      "form_guide": "",
      "comment": "ROADS END (7) turned in a better run last time to find a minor placing (24.87) at Traralgon behind Daintree Damage in a Grade 5. Chased the leaders and with a clean run can be prominent. Expected to feature in the finish again. BAYWARA (8) was prominent throughout when winning two back but could manage only midfield last time when 5th and beaten 8 lengths at Traralgon (24.67). Bold showing expected. GOT FLAIR (1) turned in a solid run last start over 300m at Healesville finishing 5th and beaten only 2.5 lengths (17.01). Solid record here at the distance winning three races. Some good form is emerging from his last run. Should play a prominent role. SHANK'S PONY (2) should be thereabouts.",
